css='body{background:#f7f6f0;color:#153f35;font:15px/1.55 system-ui;margin:auto;max-width:1080px;padding:40px}h1{font:40px Georgia}h2{font:23px Georgia;margin:26px 0 10px}p{margin:0 0 12px}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:12px}td,th{border-bottom:1px solid #dce1d8;padding:12px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top}details{margin:10px 0;background:white;padding:15px}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:12px}.muted{font-size:12px;color:#626d66}@media print{body{background:white;padding:0;font-size:11px}h1{font-size:28px}td,th{padding:6px}table{font-size:9px}}'
parts=['<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Maison Rue · Project appendix</title><style>'+css+'</style><body><p class="muted">HEC MSc DSAIB · CASE 01</p><h1>Maison Rue</h1><h2>What we built</h2><p>A small drafting assistant for the shop’s two support colleagues. It reads an enquiry against the provided policies and order snapshot, drafts a reply in the customer’s language and separates supporting facts, missing information and proposed next steps.</p><h2>Design and value</h2><p>EDGE: Efficiency. Our target is less time spent finding facts and drafting, while preserving complete, supported replies. We have not measured human time savings yet. Our main quality measure is a complete reply with correct clarification or referral and no unauthorised commitment.</p><p>5A: Assistant, delivered through an application. Enquiry → approved facts → structured response → source validation → draft and human review. The model adds language and multi-question interpretation. The baseline is a simple first-topic keyword template with the same facts; it is not a measured professional support workflow.</p><p>The customer supplies missing details. A support colleague reviews damage and outgoing replies. A support manager approves exceptions and refunds. All steps are proposed: no messages, refunds or payments are executed. Extra agents or live integrations would add complexity without helping this small snapshot.</p><h2>Team and reproduction</h2><p>Rémi Barbier: prototype, data setup, tests and documentation with Codex. Pauline: planned teammate, contribution to complete with her. Nicolas Trancart: participation pending confirmation. The assignment allows 1–3 students.</p><p>Local version: Python 3 and an authenticated Codex CLI account; run <code>python3 server.py</code> and open <code>http://127.0.0.1:8524</code>. Cloud source is in <code>vercel/</code>; it uses <code>openai/gpt-4.1</code> through Vercel AI Gateway with server-side authentication. Cloud responses must be tested separately from the local Codex results below.</p><p>Included: prompt, approved facts, cases, expected behaviour, raw outputs, content review, code and run instructions. The answer key is excluded from model inputs. Source quotes are checked exactly. Run <code>python3 -m unittest test_workflow test_server</code> and <code>python3 run_evaluation.py</code> locally; redo the content review after new outputs.</p><h2>Local development evidence</h2><p>M1–M5 come from the assignment; V6–V12 are labelled synthetic variations. Both methods receive the same inputs and facts. Fourteen local technical tests passed. Automated structural checks cover topics, sources and manager routing. A separate text inspection with Codex reviewed completeness and commitments; this is not independent human support acceptance.</p>',f'<p>Final local Codex batch: {r["inference"]["elapsed_seconds"]:.1f} seconds for 12 inputs, including CLI startup. Template: {r["baseline_seconds"]*1000:.2f} ms for the batch. Monetary cost and time through human acceptance are not measured. Token usage is retained in evaluation.json.</p>','<p>We refined the prompt after reading the initial outputs to remove internal notes from customer-facing replies. This is a known development set, not an unseen benchmark. Both runs are retained. These results do not establish production reliability or productivity gains.</p><table><tr><th>Case / input</th><th>Expected behaviour</th><th>Template result</th><th>Assistant result</th></tr>']
for row in r['rows']:
 id=row['id'];cells=[id+' · '+row['input'],row['expected']['checks'],('Pass' if a[id]['baseline']['pass'] else 'Needs work')+': '+notes[id][0],('Pass' if a[id]['prototype']['pass'] else 'Needs work')+': '+notes[id][1]]
 parts.append('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+E(c)+'</td>' for c in cells)+'</tr>')
